   631	
   632	    # --- plan-side entries OUTSIDE the manifest directory ---
   633	    # Everything inside the manifest directory is content-pinned (sha256 of
   634	    # the manifest in the signed verdict + shasum -c + name equality below).
   635	    # An EVIDENCE_PREFIX entry outside it closes by NAME ONLY — the plan file
   636	    # itself, immutable repass history, or ANOTHER tag's verdict-fields could
   637	    # be allowlisted and a post-review edit would ride the tag. The one such
   638	    # file the plan promises is the verdict-fields for THIS tag, at its ONE
   639	    # canonical path: directly inside the plan directory that CONTAINS the
   640	    # manifest dir. A basename-only rule would admit any number of
   641	    # look-alikes anywhere under EVIDENCE_PREFIX (plans/archive/, a sibling
   642	    # repass dir, ...), each an unpinned name-only pass-through. Mirror this
   643	    # rule in the W1 server-side port.
