   406	                        (explicit flags always win). Missing/invalid state
   407	                        falls back to the ADR-155 drift-classifier path —
   408	                        never an error, never a no-op.
   409	  --harness <c|codex>   PLAN-155 Wave 5: override the harness. Defaults to the
   410	                        recorded request.harness (B2 replay). When codex, the
   411	                        upgrade also refreshes the .codex/ bundle from the
   412	                        current templates (collision behavior follows
   413	                        --on-conflict; refuse leaves local edits).
   414	  --managed-hooks       PLAN-155 Wave 5 (codex): also refresh requirements.toml
   415	                        (managed-hooks posture). Replayed from state otherwise.
   416	  --skip <glob>         Exclude files from the overwrite (repeat for multiple globs).
   417	                        Example: --skip='.claude/scripts/local/*'
   418	  --skip=<glob>         Alternate inline syntax for --skip.
   419	  --purge-misinstalled  PLAN-161 U3 (opt-in — NEVER default): delete files found
   420	                        inside the framework-internal excluded trees
   421	                        (.claude/hooks/{tests,legacy}, .claude/scripts/tests,
   422	                        .claude/hooks/_lib/tests + test_isolation.py/testing.py)
   423	                        ONLY when their sha256 matches the current framework
   424	                        source at the SAME relpath or the recorded baseline
   425	                        digest for that relpath. Every purged file is backed up
   426	                        to .claude.bak/ first; symlinks are never followed.
   427	                        Without this flag (and always under --dry-run) the scan
   428	                        only PREVIEWS would-purge candidates.
   429	  --on-conflict <mode>  PLAN-138 Wave C (ADR-155): how to handle a CONFLICT — a
   430	                        file that differs from BOTH the recorded install
   431	                        baseline AND the new framework source (adopter and
   432	                        framework both changed it). One of:
   433	                          refuse  (default) per-file skip + report, never abort
   434	                          theirs  overwrite with the framework version
   435	                          backup  overwrite, original preserved in .claude.bak/
   436	                        Requires a baseline manifest; without one the upgrade
   437	                        falls back to today's diff -q warn-then-clobber.
   438	  -h, --help            Show this help and exit 0.
   439	
   440	Backup behavior:
   441	  Files about to be overwritten are first copied to .claude.bak/{timestamp}/
   442	  inside $TARGET. If a customization exists at the destination, a `diff -q`
   443	  WARNING is emitted on stderr (suppressible via --no-diff-warn).
   444	
   445	Exit codes:
   446	  0 — upgrade completed (or --help / --dry-run preview)
   447	  1 — bad usage / unknown option / missing target
   448	  2 — target has uncommitted .claude/ changes when --pin was passed
   449	
   450	Notes:
   451	  Run after `git pull` in the source ceo-orchestration repo. The upgrade
   452	  refreshes the PROTOCOL.md pointer to keep the adopter aligned with the
   453	  current source layout (DevOps-P1-4).
   454	
   455	See also:
   456	  scripts/install.sh --help     for fresh-install flags + profile semantics
   457	  INSTALL.md §Upgrade flow      for the full upgrade walk-through
   458	HELP
   459	      exit 0
   460	      ;;
   461	    -*)
   462	      echo "ERROR: unknown option: $1" >&2
   463	      exit 1
   464	      ;;
   465	    *)
   466	      TARGET="$1"
   640	  and earlier — a match refreshes it, anything else is preserved in
   641	  place with a named WARNING (ADR-155-AMEND-1).
   642	- `.claude/.framework-version` — the framework version marker, rewritten
   643	  to the source version on every upgrade (this is what
   644	  `check-framework-updates.sh` and forensic triage read post-upgrade).
   645	
   646	What is **NOT** touched (user data):
   647	
   648	- `CLAUDE.md`, `MEMORY.md`
   649	- `.claude/agent-metrics.md`
   650	- `VERSION` (root) — **deliberately**: `install.sh` is skip-if-exists,
   651	  so on an adopter repo with its own `VERSION` the framework never
   652	  wrote there, and an upgrade overwrite would take the adopter's file
   653	  (the S238/ADR-155 class). The root `VERSION` is an install-time
   654	  snapshot forever; the current framework version lives in
   655	  `.claude/.framework-version`. Do not "fix" this asymmetry — see
   656	  `ADR-155-AMEND-1`.
   657	
   658	Ceremony on upgrade: `upgrade.sh` reads the recorded install ceremony
   659	from `.claude/.install-state.json` with a dedicated reader that runs
   660	even under `--no-replay`. **Installs without a readable
   661	`.install-state.json` (all pre-Wave-B installs) are treated as
   662	`user` on upgrade** — the fail-SAFE default since the rc.4 re-pass
   663	(root PROTOCOL/SPEC/.gitignore delivery is SKIPPED, loudly). A
   664	pre-state MAINTAINER install opts back in with
   665	`upgrade.sh <target> --ceremony maintainer` (or the
   666	`CEO_UPGRADE_CEREMONY=maintainer` env override); an EXPLICIT choice is
   667	PERSISTED into the synthesized state so later upgrades recover it,
   668	while the fail-safe inference itself is never persisted — a missed
   669	flag on one run stays recoverable on the next. If your install was `--ceremony user` and
   670	predates the state file, the default already protects you; you may
   671	also re-run `install.sh --ceremony user` once so the ceremony is
   672	recorded before upgrading.
   673	
   674	`.claude/settings.json` is a special case since v1.2.0: `upgrade.sh` runs a
   675	3-state per-leaf-key **baseline migration** on it (e.g. the pair-rail
   676	registration-timeout cap 150 → 210 s, ADR-110-AMEND-2). A key is only
   677	changed when it still holds the old framework default — operator-chosen
   678	values are preserved — and the pre-migration file is copied to
   679	`.claude.bak/<timestamp>/` first.
   680	
   681	Run `bash scripts/upgrade.sh --help` for the full flag list. Key
   682	flags:
   683	
   684	- `--pin <tag>` — pin source to a specific tag/SHA (refuses if
   685	  target has uncommitted `.claude/` changes; the pin is the audit
   686	  anchor for what was actually installed).
   687	- `--dry-run` — preview what WOULD be replaced.
   688	- `--skip <glob>` — exclude files from the overwrite (repeatable).
   689	  Use this to protect adopter customizations to specific framework
   690	  scripts (e.g. `--skip='.claude/scripts/local/*'`).

