1. SEVERITY: P1  
   FILE:LINE: [scripts/upgrade.sh:3028](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3028), [scripts/upgrade.sh:3046](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3046)  
   Concrete failure: `_refresh_schema_doc` hashes and copies through destination symlinks without checking the leaf or parents. A supported `install.sh --link` installation creates schema-file symlinks ([scripts/install.sh:898](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/install.sh:898)). Upgrading it from a newer checkout can recognize the old referent as a prior generation and `cp` new content through the symlink, modifying the old source checkout outside the adopter target. A symlinked `.claude/plans` ancestor gives the same escape.  
   Minimal fix: reject symlinked ancestors and leafs before reading or writing. For provenance-authorized LINK records, replace the link itself atomically; never overwrite its referent. Add link-mode and hostile-ancestor positive controls.

2. SEVERITY: P1  
   FILE:LINE: [scripts/upgrade.sh:3025](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3025), [scripts/upgrade.sh:416](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:416)  
   Concrete failure: the new schema refresh never calls `_path_is_skipped`. `upgrade.sh target --skip='.claude/plans/DEBATE-SCHEMA.md'` still replaces a pristine prior-generation schema, violating the documented “exclude files from overwrite” contract.  
   Minimal fix: check `_path_is_skipped "$_rsd_rel"` before any inspection or write, including an accurate dry-run message; add a byte-preservation regression test.

3. SEVERITY: P1  
   FILE:LINE: [scripts/upgrade.sh:3036](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3036), [scripts/_hash_lib.sh:46](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.9Lz3fL/wt/scripts/_hash_lib.sh:46)  
   Concrete failure: schema refresh calls `shasum` directly despite the project’s shared macOS/Linux abstraction. On a supported Linux host with `sha256sum` but no Perl `shasum`, `set -euo pipefail` aborts the upgrade while inspecting an existing schema.  
   Minimal fix: use `_hash_file`; if no hasher is available, preserve the schema with a visible warning because ownership cannot be proven. Add a PATH-controlled `sha256sum`-only test.

